      "id": "math1110-limits-definition-001",
      "front": "What does \\(\\lim_{x\\to a}f(x)=L\\) say about \\(f(a)\\)?",
      "back": "It describes values of \\(f(x)\\) as \\(x\\) approaches \\(a\\); \\(f(a)\\) may differ or be undefined.",
      "tags": [
        "limits",
        "concept"
      ],
      "origin": "authored",
      "source_ref": "Guichard §2.3"
    },
    {
      "id": "math1110-continuity-test-001",
      "front": "What three conditions make \\(f\\) continuous at \\(x=a\\)?",
      "back": "\\(f(a)\\) exists; \\(\\lim_{x\\to a}f(x)\\) exists; and the limit equals \\(f(a)\\).",
      "tags": [
        "continuity",
        "definition"
      ],
      "origin": "authored",
      "source_ref": "Guichard §2.3 / §2.5"
    },
    {
      "id": "math1110-derivative-definition-001",
      "front": "How is \\(f'(a)\\) defined using a limit?",
      "back": "\\(f'(a)=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{f(a+h)-f(a)}{h}\\), if this limit exists.",
      "tags": [
        "derivative_definition",
        "definition"
